The goal of this notebook is to create the dataset for the playlist creator. While one already exists that is quite expansive it is no a few years out of date, and isn't representative of the music I would listen to. For example a one of the most popular songs on the dataset is are readings of Ernest Hemingway in Russion. So the goal here is to create a new dataset about songs more mainstream and around the bubble I listen to, and the ability of add new songs.

First we will be creating a catalog of all authors, with data on their popularity and number of collaborators. Preliminarily data will only be collected on the first 5000 artists come from BFS starting at Kanye West: essentially get list of all collaborators then append to the end and loop through. 

After the count of collaborators and popularity has been completed for this set, we can look at the collaborators of the most popular artists and add them to the list.

Then investigate the distribution of artist popularity to determine a threshold, where only artists above this threshold will have their songs included in the dataset.


